          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. You know that the sum of angles of a quadrilateral is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 6 0 ^ { \\circ }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , even for a non-convex quadrilateral. (Recall the proof.) Now consider a self-intersecting quadrilateral ABCD, where AB and CD intersect at point E. Show that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle A + \\angle B + \\angle C + \\angle D < 360^{\\circ}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Can you construct ABCD such that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle A + \\angle B + \\angle C + \\angle D = 2^{\\circ}?"
            }
          ]
        },
